WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.940
1967

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:21.580
Mankind makes first contact with 
an extraterrestrial life form

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.460
that we had earlier identified on Mars.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.490
The BETA: Being of Extra Terrestrial origin 
which is an Adversary of the human race.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:10.420
Mankind used all the technology it 
had in its defense against the BETA.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:12.420
However...

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.160
The First Lunar Surface War

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.920
1973

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.970
We were unable to stop the BETA
from reaching Earth.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:07.650
This story is but one chapter

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:12.450
in the tale of the fight against 
the ever-expanding BETA incursion.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.740
1997

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.130
Capital of Imperial Japan - Kyoto

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.130
Oh, here she comes!

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.910
Coming to school reading a textbook again?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.130
Yui!

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:53.580
Hey, Yui!

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.490
Good day.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.610
Good day.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.990
Same as always, huh?

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.300
Everyone, look!

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.930
Once we graduate, that’s 
what we’ll be piloting.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:26.500
The Zuikaku Type-82 Tactical Surface Fighter!

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:33.170
Wasn’t the Zuikaku the 
unit your father helped develop?

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.220
Yes…

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:42.240
The Imperial Capital Burns - Part 1

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.240
Imperial Guard Training Academy

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.870
8 Minutes

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.870
8 minutes.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:59.650
This is the average time a soldier manages to 
survive even after their first victory against the BETA.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:05.400
Only after overcoming this hurdle can 
you begin to become a true soldier.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.320
Listen up.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.220
I’ll say it again.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.660
Hey, want to go somewhere after school?

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.160
They cannot understand any 
language from any nation.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.330
I didn’t get any sleep...

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.300
The rules that apply between 
humans don't apply to them!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.970
Up late talking to your boyfriend again?

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:19.070
Your enemy is the BETA, the first 
extraterrestrial species mankind has encountered.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.680
He says he’s getting 
reassigned to Kyushu soon.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.820
Kyushu?

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.120
Didn’t they order evacuation 
of the whole island last year?

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:25.080
This is nothing like the wars started by 
England’s King or the Corsican Monster.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.740
He wouldn’t tell me all the details,

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.940
but apparently a new base was established.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.780
Ever since we made first 
contact with then in 1967,

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.830
Huh? Really?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.280
we've been dragged back into the ice age...

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.240
Hey, we’re in the middle of lecture.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:32.250
You there!

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.250
Y-Yes!

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.980
Takamura…Yui.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.770
Takamura?

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.100
Oh? A member of the Takamura family, one 
of our Shogun’s hereditary vassals.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.400
Then Cadet Takamura.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.260
Where does the name BETA come from?

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:53.110
Yes. They are extraterrestrial beings 
opposing the human race, in other words-

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:59.140
Being of Extra Terrestrial origin 
which is an Adversary of the human race.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.520
Fine, sit down.We’re 
continuing the lecture.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.890
That was Yamashiro-san, wasn’t it?

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.610
The Yamashiro family.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:24.420
If I recall, they’ve turned out a great number of 
pilots, despite not being one of the Shogun's vassals.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:29.080
I see, so that’s why they’d 
view Yui and her family as a rival.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:30.290
Huh?

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:33.220
Aww, come on...

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.330
A rival?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.140
Oh? “I’ll be able to come 
home to you on my next leave”?

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.060
Don’t peek!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.700
Same Year - Fall

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.380
In accordance with this, the Asian Union 
has erected an absolute defense line

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.020
Speaking of which, Yui, 
is your dad still abroad?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:59.020
to prevent the BETA from invading Japan.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.910
It seems he comes and goes.

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:04.910
Meanwhile, Australia and 
Brazil have announced

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.200
Even when he comes back 
to Japan, he stays in Tokyo.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:08.980
that they will accept refugees from 
the People’s Republic of China...

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.230
That car looks expensive!

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.050
In times like these, those 
of you in military families

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:20.280
should take the initiative and set an 
example of frugality for the common citizens!

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.810
Was that supposed to be our instructor?

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:24.140
Did I sound like him?

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.330
Very!

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.000
That’s…

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.300
I have a message from him.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.820
He sends his best regards.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.530
I’m home!

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:43.440
Oh, welcome home.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.340
I knew it was you, uncle!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.550
Oh, pardon me!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.080
Lt. Col. Iwaya!

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:54.330
Oh my, what a splendid salute.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:59.990
When did the cute young lady I knew 
grow up to be such a splendid soldier?

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.170
You haven't been commissioned yet,

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.610
and we’re in private.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.730
So you can act like normal.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.870
Yes! Uncle!

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:11.470
I’m surprised you knew I was here.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.270
Well, with all those cars…

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:20.000
Given the times, I turned them 
down to be frugal as well, but…

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:33.080
He told you to strive hard in your training.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.900
Apparently he won’t be able 
to leave Ichigaya for a while.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.740
So the situation on the mainland is…

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.580
It’s not good.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.880
Oh, that's right.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.360
Senna-san told me you’re finally going 
to start your live training, aren’t you?

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.360
Yes!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:57.310
In the Imperial Guard Training 
Academy our training unit is the Gekishin.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.770
Once you graduate you’ll 
be piloting the Zuikaku.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.970
Both are good units, but eventually…

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:04.870
Eventually?

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.080
We can’t afford to let them 
overrun our beautiful nation.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:21.160
Right now we need all the good TSFs we can get.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:25.160
Please wait a little longer. 
Soon I’ll be joining too.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.050
Don’t misunderstand me.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:27.700
Huh?

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.390
Our nation is important, but…

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:40.140
We’re all doing our jobs, praying that young 
girls like you never have to see the front lines.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.820
You must not be hasty.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:43.900
Yes.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.980
I suppose it’s time for me to go.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.800
How long will you be staying in Kyoto?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.920
Once I finish my business here I’ll 
be flying right back to Tokyo.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.030
I see…

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:03.870
It’s a shame I won’t get to eat any of 
the meat stew Senna-san’s so proud of.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.500
Then next time, I’ll make it!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.360
I’ll be looking forward to it.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.820
The autumn sky in Japan is lovely.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.010
Yes, it really is.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:27.460
Koubuin Family Mansion

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:28.050
My apologizes for taking up your time when you're so busy.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:32.420
No, I was the one who asked 
to speak with you, plus…

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.670
I wanted to come and see 
how Kyoto was faring.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:40.940
So, why have you come to our house 
out of the five regent houses?

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:42.490
Before that…

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.750
If you could please have a look at the 
progress on the matter we discussed.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:04.190
"In war, then, let your great object 
be victory, not lengthy campaigns."

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:07.870
Sun Tzu?

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:14.610
I pray that these new weapons will allow 
us to bring a swift end to this war.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:18.160
I believe they will.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.670
Type 99 EM Radiation Cannon Plans

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.310
This is so tight!

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.780
Why don’t you go up a 
size instead of forcing it?

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.960
Once it's skin-tight you'll 
stop thinking about it.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:47.220
But aren’t these enhancement 
suits a little embarrassing?

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:49.550
Yeah, with your childish body they are.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.450
At last…

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:08.690
The Tactical Surface Fighter, or TSF for 
short, is both your weapon and armor!

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.680
First you need to learn how to use it 
like an extension of your own body.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:25.050
Listen up! Fly low and fast, like 
you’re stuck to the ground!

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.690
Altitude Warning

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.360
Unit 6! You’re too high!

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.680
Do you want to get burnt to 
a crisp by a Laser Class?

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.170
Shift to mobile formation!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.270
Advance towards the enemy!

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.950
Switch to formation Wedge 1 at 3000m!

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:51.330
Attack formation Wedge 1!

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.310
What's wrong with you?

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.650
Are you trying to damage our precious TSFs?

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:14.590
You’re all dead, return 
and give me 10 laps!

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:16.680
What?

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:29.070
Wait up, everyone!

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:51.830
Put your back into it!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.990
Don’t give up even if you’re 
the last one standing!

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:57.660
Those who give up are the first 
to die on the battlefield!

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.000
Come on! What’s wrong?

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:12.320
Is that all you've got, Takamura-san?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.190
This ends it!

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:25.550
What?

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.420
Why you!

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.470
Takamura, one point!

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:41.980
She did it!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.530
Good job!

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:50.930
Umm…

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:53.300
If you’d like…

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.410
I'll take it.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:02.680
Thanks.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.980
Thank you very much!

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:09.940
Did you see that guy’s face?!

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:11.850
Hey, Aki, you’re laughing too much.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:12.690
She’s right.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.670
Yamashiro-san, what’s your first name?

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.060
Let me have one of those too.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:15.130
Here.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:16.990
Oh, it’s read “Kazusa”.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:18.520
Hey, Yui, this is delicious! Here, try some!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.200
What middle school did you go to?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.220
Anyone who's scared, leave 
and don't come back!

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:28.560
The only people we need here 
are those with a strong will!

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:43.580
1998

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:48.160
Korean Peninsula

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.970
Ichigaya - Imperial Ministry of Technology

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:03.140
Yes, patch it through.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:04.710
It’s me.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.150
I see. Alright.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:12.610
Continue sending me the 
information as it comes in.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.800
So the mainland has fallen at last?

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.340
Soon Japan will...

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:33.000
Izumo, Flagship of the 
Imperial Navy's 6th Fleet

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:40.630
BETA vanguard entering Tsushima Strait 
off the southern tip of the Korean Peninsula.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:41.760
Countless more following behind them.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.560
A divine wind, huh?

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:45.410
Sir?

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:51.360
We didn't deploy enough ships to 
stop their advance after all.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.280
Because of this typhoon none of the 
other ships in the combined fleet can…

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:58.780
If we let them make land, there will 
be tens of thousands of casualties.

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:04.630
July

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.400
BETA - Landing in Northern Kyushu

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:36.880
No!

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.220
What’s wrong?

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.160
Her boyfriend who was 
assigned to Kyushu, well…

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:48.240
My cousin and his wife both lived in Tottori.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:50.650
They say they weren’t 
able to evacuate in time…

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.310
We repeat.

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:58.100
As the BETA advance from the 
northern Kyushu and San'in

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:01.700
towards the center of Japan,

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:05.610
Emergency:  Beta Invasion!

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:05.680
the Imperial Japanese Army, along 
with the UN and American militaries,

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:09.390
has decided to create a combined defense line

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:13.070
in the area in front of the capital city, 
Kyoto, which bridges Maidzuru and Kobe.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:13.050
Combined Defense Line

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:17.750
Furthermore, new evacuation advisories

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.640
Our next step after training is this?

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:19.500
Even we can do some good.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:19.500
have been issued for the following regions:

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.000
the Osaka metropolitan area,

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.500
Shiga prefecture,

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.030
Nara prefecture,

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.010
Wakayama prefecture,

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.370
Mie prefecture,

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.390
Aichi prefecture...

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.350
I’m going back to Kyoto!

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.000
Dad?

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:42.770
If we lose our capital, it 
won't matter where we run!

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.170
Dad!

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.270
Miss!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:28.690
Serve the nation and its people in a way 
that's worthy of the Takamura family name.

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:32.880
I’m heading off.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.940
July 31st

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:43.070
Kyoto - Final Defense Line

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:06.500
Mobile Scout Squad 27 has met and engaged 
BETA group 3-B 6km west of Maidzuru.

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:08.660
Unmanned scouts D-21 and A-19 have 
been shot down by Laser Class!

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:09.720
Combat confirmed near Fukuchiyama!

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:10.960
Still more squads are engaging the enemy!

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:19.220
 Arashiyama, Kyoto - Temporary Supply Base

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:19.220
Your mission is to protect this 
supply base with your lives!

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:26.530
You students have no combat experience 
and barely any training.

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:29.620
If you go out there, you’ll only get 
in the way of our regular soldiers!

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:33.710
Right now, focus only 
on defending this place!

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.570
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:38.980
Get in the way, huh?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.480
That may be true, but…

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:46.630
I wanted to get revenge for my boyfriend…

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:49.560
Everyone, this is serious.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:55.250
A BETA vanguard has broken through 
all the way to Takagamine.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.380
Takagamine?

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:57.740
That’s right next to us!

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:03.590
How?

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.630
What about the defense line?

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.530
It was eaten apart.

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:13.500
Hey, that’s...

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:15.980
Resupply?

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:17.440
No…

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:21.160
Laser Class!

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:33.640
When was it?

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:37.690
When did the living stop counting the dead?

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:43.910
Is this world truly walking 
the path to extinction?

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:52.230
A BETA scout vanguard 
is approaching 10km to our west!

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:53.760
Condition Red!

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.000
All pilots, hurry and board your TSFs!

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.550
I repeat…

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:00.620
They’re advancing too fast!

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:04.240
How? This is a supply base 
nowhere near the front line!

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:07.530
No…

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.370
This is the front line now.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:13.140
Start the engines!

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:34.170
That BETA scout group is still approaching!

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:36.920
Roughly 220 in number!

00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:39.060
Destroyer Class at the head,

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.790
followed by Grappler Class!

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.470
Laser Class spotted in the rear!

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:55.080
Father, please watch over us.

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:57.210
Blast off!

00:24:06.550 --> 00:24:07.190
Please...

00:24:08.560 --> 00:24:09.160
shoot…

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:11.690
me…

00:24:12.520 --> 00:24:13.440
hurry!

00:24:17.250 --> 00:24:19.210
Next Tim on Total Eclipse:

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:21.920
The Imperial Capital Burns, Part 2
